WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.390
I am aware that I inhale, I am aware that I exhale, I am my breath, I become aware of my body, I relax my body, I generate

2
00:00:10.390 --> 00:00:14.810
a feeling of joy, I generate a feeling of happiness in the present.

3
00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:22.370
I become aware of my pain, I embrace my pain, I take care of it.

4
00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:26.900
It is important to have good motivation when you start to meditate.

5
00:00:28.067 --> 00:00:38.627
will present you with obstacles. The first obstacle you will encounter is laziness. It will bring you a second subtlety, which is called active laziness. I was doing a

6
00:00:40.007 --> 00:00:51.367
lot of things except going to meditate. A third form of laziness that still arises is abandonment. But then you tell yourself no, ultimately it's not for me. The antidote

7
00:00:52.207 --> 00:00:54.531
is to find a proper motivation.

8
00:00:54.531 --> 00:00:58.594
This motivation must be not only for yourself, but also for others.

9
00:00:58.915 --> 00:01:06.115
The second real obstacle you will encounter, is that when you learn to meditate, initially, there is a methodology in learning.

10
00:01:07.315 --> 00:01:19.764
The obstacle you will encounter is the complete forgetting of what needs to be done. At one point, I was meditating, or rather, I thought I was meditating, I was sitting there, ultimately, I was quite lost in thought.

11
00:01:19.764 --> 00:01:23.075
I understood that meditation is a training of the mind.

12
00:01:23.075 --> 00:01:26.398
It comes from a very ancient etymology which means...

13
00:01:26.398 --> 00:01:29.495
Truly learning to discover one's own functioning.

14
00:01:29.495 --> 00:01:32.750
You are not always well when you meditate, but that's okay.

15
00:01:32.750 --> 00:01:35.507
I learn to recognize, to train my mind.

16
00:01:35.507 --> 00:01:42.059
And the antidote, which I think is very interesting for us in the practice of meditation, is attention, is mindfulness.

17
00:01:42.059 --> 00:01:53.717
To discover this energy that is in your mind, this energy which is concentration, and which will gradually open you to another energy, which is the profound vision of things. But one must proceed gradually.

18
00:01:53.717 --> 00:01:58.546
It's like when you enter a space where on the walls. There are secrets that can be unveiled.

19
00:01:58.546 --> 00:02:01.634
I enter with a candle, and the candle is your mind.

20
00:02:01.634 --> 00:02:06.102
Initially, the candle flickers like this, meaning there isn't much luminosity.

21
00:02:06.102 --> 00:02:16.206
But if, through the foundational practice of your meditation, you learn to completely stabilize the flame, a kind of luminous halo appears, a clarity that emerges.

22
00:02:16.206 --> 00:02:24.606
Well, it's somewhat the same thing. If you truly manage to stabilize your mind, suddenly you will perceive a kind of luminous clarity.

23
00:02:24.606 --> 00:02:36.926
that appears in one's mind. This clarity leads you to profound insight. One must learn to stabilize the mind because it is an entire process of stabilization. Therefore, it is learning

24
00:02:36.926 --> 00:02:42.026
to develop this clarity of mind primarily through the energy of mindfulness,

25
00:02:42.026 --> 00:02:45.866
concentration, and the energy of profound insight.

26
00:02:45.866 --> 00:02:49.246
One must practice. Everyone can access this.

